course: dictionary
lesson: 8435
title: Sacred and respect
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words tell you what people believe and what they hold dear. «Sacred» is one of them. It means holy, connected with God, a god or a religion, and treated with deep respect. The words around it give you clues about which meaning is being used.
explain: «Uluru in Australia, once called Ayers Rock, is sacred to the Anangu people, and climbing it was banned in 2019 to respect them.» The word «respect» is the clue. People treat something sacred carefully, so sacred means holy and deserving deep respect. Try your meaning in the sentence: "holy, and treated with deep respect" fits.
explain: «Saturday morning is sacred to my dad.» Here sacred is not about religion. It means very important to someone, so it must not be harmed. Ask yourself: what would fit here? Then put your meaning in the sentence to check it still makes sense.
fact: Sacred means holy, or very important to someone so that it must not be harmed.
fact: «The Ganges is sacred to Hindus.» Here sacred means holy, connected with a religion.
fact: Useful phrases are sacred place, sacred text and sacred site.
fact: Sacred is an adjective, and it can change: sacred, more sacred, most sacred.
fact: «Cats were honoured as sacred in ancient Egypt.» This shows that people treated cats with deep respect.
exercise: «Climbing Uluru was banned to respect the Anangu people, because Uluru is sacred to them.» What does sacred mean here? | Very old and falling apart | Very large and high | Only used on Saturdays | *Holy, and treated with deep respect
exercise: Dad says, «Saturday morning is sacred to me.» What does he mean? | *It is very important to him, so it must not be harmed | It is the coldest time of the week | It is a holy day in a church | He always has toast then and nothing else
exercise: Find and copy one word from «The Vedas are very old sacred hymns, learned by heart.» that tells you the hymns are holy. | Vedas | hymns | *sacred | old
test: What does «sacred site» mean? | A flat, empty field | *A place that is holy or very important to people | A place where you can play football | A site for a new shop
test: «Cats were honoured as sacred in ancient Egypt.» What does this show? | Cats lived only in towns | Cats could not catch mice | Cats were thought to be a waste of time | *People treated cats with deep respect, as holy
exam: Which sentence uses sacred to mean very important to someone, not holy? | The Vedas are very old sacred hymns. | Dogs were the first tame animals. | *Saturday morning is sacred to my dad. | The Ganges is sacred to Hindus.
